@@ -111,3 +111,11 @@
 ## Cortés Combat (written 2026-10-30, NOT b1.7.3)
 
 - **Combat rework (cone reach, cooldown, charge, guard, five weapon families; healing is "Healing without hunger" above):** needs wood, cobblestone, iron, diamond, gold, sticks, flint and iron blocks (existing sources) -> weapons that kill mobs; Hooks: crafting (`craft::recipes`, recipe book), durability (`craft::max_damage`), mobs and their damage window (`mobs`), stamina (`vitals`, guard), the touch HUD (`input/touch_ui`), sound (`audio`); Overlaps: sword, axe, hoe (they get a profile of the same system, so each keeps a job: the sword is the wide cheap cone with no special, the hoe sweeps). Switch: `combatRules`, default off. Plan: [`combat.md`](combat.md).
+
+## Weapon payments and the cooldown ledger (written 2026-11-05, NOT b1.7.3, Immersive Pack worlds only; every number UNVERIFIED by play, not compiled)
+
+Each weapon pays one dominant currency (time, stamina, or risk/position) so none goes obsolete (rule 2): sword cheap and general, ropera and alabarda pay stamina, shotel pays timing, martillo pays momentum, axe pays time.
+
+- **Axe as the commitment weapon:** needs the iron, stone and wood already in the world (no new source) -> fewer, heavier blows: damage `2 x (2 + bonus)` (4, 6, 8, 10, 4), charge bonus 0.75 over 40 ticks (iron: 8, or 14 charged), the hold counts from the start of the cooldown, no stamina weight (1.0, was 1.2), and a hit staggers the mob (10 ticks, 16 charged: no steering, no bite); Hooks: `rules::swing_of`, `Profile::{charge, weight}`, charge HUD / `charge_tick`, `Mobs::stagger`; Overlaps: sword (stays the quick cheap one: iron sword ~7.7 DPS plain, axe ~80% of it per swing cycle but heavier per blow).
+- **Cooldown ledger per weapon:** needs the `swing_cd` the swing already pays -> a lunge (8 swings) or a sweep (4) stays owed when you swap away and back (`App::swing_debt`: id -> ticks left, counting down in the background), a swap costs a 6-tick draw lock (at most the new weapon's interval); Hooks: `swing_cd` in `lib.rs`, the equip animation, stamina; Overlaps: none. Parry is unaffected (`parry_cd` lives in `State`). This is option C of the proposal plus the short draw lock.
+- **Player knockback:** a hit that takes (`Vitals::hurt` true, so not one the damage window refuses, not a blocked, parried or lunging one) shoves the player away from its source: `EntityLiving.knockBack`, motion halved, 0.4 blocks a tick horizontal along the line from the attacker, vertical `min(0.4, vy / 2 + 0.4)`; the horizontal part rides in `kick` like an explosion's and ends the sprint. b1.7.3's own behaviour, so no switch; Hooks: `Ev::Hurt`, `kick`, `vitals`, `sprint`; Overlaps: guard and parry (they stop the hit, so no shove).
